Example 4: School Management (Person → Student/Teacher)

```python
class Person:
    def __init__(self, name, age):
        self.name = name
        self.age = age

class Student(Person):
    def study(self):
        print(f"{self.name} is studying")

class Teacher(Person):
    def teach(self):
        print(f"{self.name} is teaching")

s = Student("Kabir", 15)
t = Teacher("Mr. Sharma", 40)
s.study()
t.teach()
```
*Real-life link:* Hierarchical inheritance — Students and Teachers are both People, but with different roles.

