Key Takeaways

- Inheritance = **"IS-A" relationship** (a Car IS-A Vehicle).
- Use `super()` to call the parent class's constructor/methods.
- Overriding lets a child class **customize** inherited behavior.
- Python supports 5 types of inheritance — know when to use which.
- Don't overuse deep inheritance chains — keep designs simple and readable.
- Practice by mapping **real-world relationships** to classes — it makes the concept click faster!
